ogging=syslog --with-logfac=authpriv, confirmed default sudo commands were appearing in /var/log/secure\",\"Wrote /etc/sudoers.d/sudo-command-logging with 'Defaults !syslog', 'Defaults logfile=\\\"/var/log/sudo-commands.log\\\"', 'Defaults log_year, log_host'; validated with visudo -c\",\"Created /var/log/sudo-commands.log with 0600 root:root perms; confirmed SELinux context var_log_t matches /var/log/secure\",\"Ran test sudo commands and confirmed entries (with date/year, user, host, command) appear only in the new logfile and not in /var/log/secure or journalctl _COMM=sudo COMMAND= lines\",\"Cleaned up temp test artifacts\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline, triggered 'shutdown -r now' on node1 in background so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed boot_id changed (bef0e5ec... -> 6f7b9e68...), proving an actual reboot occurred\",\"Post-reboot: re-verified sudoers drop-in intact, visudo -c passes, prior log entries persisted, and a new sudo command was correctly logged to the dedicated file with no corresponding entry in /var/log/secure\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Sudo commands recorded with user and timestamp\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3aaa12b9798042c7\",\"cmd-1641ea23134f46aa\"],\"summary\":\"/var/log/sudo-commands.log entries show 'date : invoking_user : HOST=... ; PWD=...; USER=target_user ; COMMAND=...' for each sudo invocation\"},{\"requirement\":\"Entries kept out of general system log\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a9b89afc63304f5c\",\"cmd-3aaa12b9798042c7\",\"cmd-1641ea23134f46aa\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline showed COMMAND= lines in /var/log/secure before the change; after adding 'Defaults !syslog' and logfile, subsequent sudo runs produced no new COMMAND= entries in /var/log/secure\"},{\"requirement\":\"Config is valid and persists\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-21b2ef11308f48a9\",\"cmd-da586375f14c40f5\",\"cmd-f48adf7d883d4edf\"],\"summary\":\"visudo -c validated the drop-in both before install and again after reboot; file and its 3 rule lines unchanged post-restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d973204bcfea4c60\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id bef0e5ec-ce32-423b-826a-8a5a90584d3a and confirmed sudoers config + 4-line log present before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1991cd80cbcc4e44\"],\"summary\":\"'shutdown -r now' issued in background on node1; exec stream closed as expected, confirming the reboot command was accepted before disconnect\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 boot identity changed (proof of actual restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c3b2233938a847f0\",\"cmd-5bd7ea4366464c1f\",\"cmd-bc934e53341748fa\"],\"summary\":\"Node was unreachable for two poll attempts, then came back with boot_id 6f7b9e68-80d1-4017-8c56-ca75b9b6d0d3, different from the pre-restart boot_id, and a new uptime -s start time\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 post-restart recovery of required config/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f48adf7d883d4edf\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, sudoers drop-in still valid, prior log entries intact, and a fresh sudo command was correctly logged to /var/log/sudo-commands.log with no corresponding entry in /var/log/secure\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured sudo on node1 to log every sudo command (with invoking/target user and timestamp) to a dedicated /var/log/sudo-commands.log, and disabled sudo's syslog channel so those entries no longer land in the general system log (/var/log/secure or journal). Verified pre- and post-reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected baseline: RHEL9 node1, sudo 1.9.17p2 compiled with --with-logging=syslog --with-logfac=authpriv, confirmed default sudo commands were appearing in /var/log/secure","Wrote /etc/sudoers.d/sudo-command-logging with 'Defaults !syslog', 'Defaults logfile=\"/var/log/sudo-commands.log\"', 'Defaults log_year, log_host'; validated with visudo -c","Created /var/log/sudo-commands.log with 0600 root:root perms; confirmed SELinux context var_log_t matches /var/log/secure","Ran test sudo commands and confirmed entries (with date/year, user, host, command) appear only in the new logfile and not in /var/log/secure or journalctl _COMM=sudo COMMAND= lines","Cleaned up temp test artifacts","Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline, triggered 'shutdown -r now' on node1 in background so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again; confirmed boot_id changed (bef0e5ec... -> 6f7b9e68...), proving an actual reboot occurred","Post-reboot: re-verified sudoers drop-in intact, visudo -c passes, prior log entries persisted, and a new sudo command was correctly logged to the dedicated file with no corresponding entry in /var/log/secure"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Sudo commands recorded with user and timestamp","command_ids":["cmd-3aaa12b9798042c7","cmd-1641ea23134f46aa"],"summary":"/var/log/sudo-commands.log entries show 'date : invoking_user : HOST=... ; PWD=...; USER=target_user ; COMMAND=...' for each sudo invocation"},{"requirement":"Entries kept out of general system log","command_ids":["cmd-a9b89afc63304f5c","cmd-3aaa12b9798042c7","cmd-1641ea23134f46aa"],"summary":"Baseline showed COMMAND= lines in /var/log/secure before the change; after adding 'Defaults !syslog' and logfile, subsequent sudo runs produced no new COMMAND= entries in /var/log/secure"},{"requirement":"Config is valid and persists","command_ids":["cmd-21b2ef11308f48a9","cmd-da586375f14c40f5","cmd-f48adf7d883d4edf"],"summary":"visudo -c validated the drop-in both before install and again after reboot; file and its 3 rule lines unchanged post-restart"},{"requirement":"Node1 baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-d973204bcfea4c60"],"summary":"Captured boot_id bef0e5ec-ce32-423b-826a-8a5a90584d3a and confirmed sudoers config + 4-line log present before reboot"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement","command_ids":["cmd-1991cd80cbcc4e44"],"summary":"'shutdown -r now' issued in background on node1; exec stream closed as expected, confirming the reboot command was accepted before disconnect"},{"requirement":"Node1 boot identity changed (proof of actual restart)","command_ids":["cmd-c3b2233938a847f0","cmd-5bd7ea4366464c1f","cmd-bc934e53341748fa"],"summary":"Node was unreachable for two poll attempts, then came back with boot_id 6f7b9e68-80d1-4017-8c56-ca75b9b6d0d3, different from the pre-restart boot_id, and a new uptime -s start time"},{"requirement":"Node1 post-restart recovery of required config/data","command_ids":["cmd-f48adf7d883d4edf"],"summary":"After reboot, sudoers drop-in still valid, prior log entries intact, and a fresh sudo command was correctly logged to /var/log/sudo-commands.log with no corresponding entry in /var/log/secure"}]},"ttft_ms":1776,"type":"result","duration_ms":87471,"uuid":"b1f35a0c-e039-47be-965c-2e7394c099ff","ttft_stream_ms":1436,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":1436,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
